    <string name="tutorial_cable_title">Lay a cable</string>
    <string name="tutorial_cable_text">The PC wants to send a mail. Drag with your finger from the PC to the mail server.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_router_title">Place a router</string>
    <string name="tutorial_router_text">A device has only 2 ports, a router has 6. Tap “Router” below, then a free cell near the phones.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_router_connect_text">Now connect both phones and the phone exchange to the router. It shares out the calls.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_bandwidth_title">Bandwidth</string>
    <string name="tutorial_bandwidth_text">1998: The TV wants to stream. Connect it to the streaming server.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_bandwidth_narrow_text">Too narrow! Streaming needs bandwidth %1$d, ISDN carries only %2$d. Pick DSL below, it carries %3$d.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_bandwidth_upgrade_text">Now tap the ISDN cable to upgrade it to DSL. You only pay the difference.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_ping_title">Ping</string>
    <string name="tutorial_ping_text">2010: The PC wants to play online. Gaming needs a short ping, at most %1$d ms there and back. Connect the PC to the game server.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_ping_slow_text">Ping %1$d ms: too slow for gaming (at most %2$d ms). Only fiber is fast enough. Pick fiber and tap the cable.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_overload_title">Overload</string>
    <plurals name="tutorial_overload_text">
        <item quantity="one">A new PC without a connection! From %1$d waiting request on, a red ring fills up. When it closes, the game is over. Connect the PC!</item>
        <item quantity="other">A new PC without a connection! From %1$d waiting requests on, a red ring fills up. When it closes, the game is over. Connect the PC!</item>
    </plurals>
    <string name="tutorial_done_title">Well done!</string>
    <string name="tutorial_done_text">You know the basics. Tips: tap a server to upgrade it, tap a cable twice to remove it, and pause stops the clock while you keep building. Have fun!</string>
